1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,920
how did your mock exam go pretty well i'd say i've had fun this year but i've also studied a lot

2
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:17,800
such as the life of a senior when i get home i review my lessons and old exam questions

3
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:22,380
in my spare time i memorize vocabulary and formulas

4
00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:27,900
though my daily grind is tough i do have a singular reprieve

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,960
and that's reading manga the highlight of my whole week

6
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:43,740
he's a double agent but how i never even saw it coming why did this slice of life chapter take a turn

7
00:00:43,740 --> 00:00:46,320
you're killing me

8
00:00:46,320 --> 00:00:51,320
next week can't come soon enough

9
00:00:51,320 --> 00:01:05,660
you

10
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:35,640
Thank you.

11
00:01:35,660 --> 00:02:05,640
Thank you.

12
00:02:05,660 --> 00:02:35,640
Thank you.

13
00:02:35,660 --> 00:02:48,280
Kono Ha's new chapter.

14
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:53,820
Um, pardon me.

15
00:02:54,220 --> 00:02:56,200
Did the latest weekly Shino be coming today?

16
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:57,400
Uh, yeah?

17
00:02:58,280 --> 00:03:00,180
We sold out of it a few minutes ago.

18
00:03:03,840 --> 00:03:05,240
Wanna back order one?

19
00:03:05,780 --> 00:03:06,720
Uh-oh.

20
00:03:08,720 --> 00:03:11,420
Convenience stores always sell out on release day.

21
00:03:11,580 --> 00:03:15,400
But even the bookstore didn't have Kuroha's new chapter.

22
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:24,640
Why, after thinking about Kuroha all day, have I just died from this disappointment?

23
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:26,740
Huh? That you, Kono?

24
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:33,520
Oh, yep, sure is. Hey there. He witnessed my cringiness.

25
00:03:34,140 --> 00:03:36,440
So you came here for the latest weekly Shinobi?

26
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:38,400
Are you psychic or something?

27
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:43,240
Don't I wish. I heard you say Konoha's new chapter. And you sounded upset.

28
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:43,840
Ah!

29
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:46,860
How embarrassing.

30
00:03:46,860 --> 00:03:50,300
Um, you can have mine, if you'd like.

31
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:54,320
Hasn't even been cracked open yet.

32
00:03:56,060 --> 00:03:57,020
I can't!

33
00:03:57,240 --> 00:04:00,460
Why? If you're fretting because you're worried about me, please don't.

34
00:04:01,060 --> 00:04:04,420
I'll be fine. Gata would have bought it if it hadn't been the last copy.

35
00:04:04,980 --> 00:04:07,740
I just came in here to kill some time until my bus arrives.

36
00:04:07,740 --> 00:04:13,160
There are lots of bookstores near the station by my house. They can't all be sold out.

37
00:04:14,360 --> 00:04:17,080
Sorry to cut this short, but I should go before I miss my bus.

38
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:18,600
Wow! Thanks a million!

39
00:04:19,540 --> 00:04:21,280
I'll pay you back first thing tomorrow.

40
00:04:22,140 --> 00:04:23,960
You are so cool. And kind.

41
00:04:24,420 --> 00:04:25,460
The way you helped me out.

42
00:04:25,460 --> 00:04:27,920
You're just like Kono.

43
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:28,020
You're just like Kono.

44
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:34,820
Thank you very much.

45
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:36,800
Awkward.

46
00:04:37,380 --> 00:04:40,380
Did comparing him to one of the characters rub him the wrong way?

47
00:04:40,880 --> 00:04:42,500
Why'd I even open my mouth?

48
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:50,040
I remind her of a fictional lady?

49
00:04:50,740 --> 00:04:52,920
Does she say that because she thinks I'm effeminate?

50
00:04:53,700 --> 00:04:54,760
Oh, man.

51
00:04:55,940 --> 00:04:58,900
I weirded him out with silly fangirl nonsense.

52
00:04:59,860 --> 00:05:00,080
What?

53
00:05:07,840 --> 00:05:10,480
I guess Yanagi's a fan in his own right.

54
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:24,360
It's weekly Shinobi release day today.

55
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:24,420
It's weekly Shinobi release day today.

56
00:05:27,700 --> 00:05:29,720
Kono has been so exciting lately.

57
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:31,200
I can't put it down.

58
00:05:31,660 --> 00:05:32,780
I can't blame you.

59
00:05:33,260 --> 00:05:35,280
Normally, I'll wait for the full book publication.

60
00:05:35,660 --> 00:05:37,300
But once I read a manga and a magazine,

61
00:05:37,660 --> 00:05:39,200
patience gives way to curiosity.

62
00:05:39,440 --> 00:05:40,520
Every time.

63
00:05:40,660 --> 00:05:41,960
Talk about an odd pair.

64
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:46,020
I haven't heard that in a while.

65
00:05:46,340 --> 00:05:48,620
No one makes those comments when I'm with Hori's group.

66
00:05:50,420 --> 00:05:52,380
Maybe you aren't, Link?

67
00:05:52,560 --> 00:05:53,820
Are you upset with me?

68
00:05:54,040 --> 00:05:55,000
No, not at all.

69
00:05:55,060 --> 00:05:56,500
It's just, uh...

70
00:05:56,500 --> 00:05:58,800
When I'm by you, girls get jealous.

71
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:01,800
They just can't fathom why on earth you'd spend time with me.

72
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:02,240
Eh.

73
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:03,960
Hmm?

74
00:06:04,880 --> 00:06:06,080
And why is that?

75
00:06:06,080 --> 00:06:08,900
Because you're cool and I'm not?

76
00:06:10,300 --> 00:06:10,740
Cool?

77
00:06:10,740 --> 00:06:10,820
Cool?

78
00:06:11,820 --> 00:06:14,800
Oh, Remy got a nasty paper cut.

79
00:06:14,920 --> 00:06:16,440
Try thinking about something fun.

80
00:06:16,940 --> 00:06:18,560
Like how school gets out early today.

81
00:06:18,820 --> 00:06:19,260
Yay!

82
00:06:19,260 --> 00:06:21,480
It's gone now.

83
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:23,660
Don't cry over a harmless little bug.

84
00:06:23,980 --> 00:06:25,020
I'm not crying.

85
00:06:25,580 --> 00:06:27,180
But it's really gone.

86
00:06:27,440 --> 00:06:27,960
You're sure?

87
00:06:28,420 --> 00:06:30,040
You're cooler than me by far.

88
00:06:30,180 --> 00:06:30,360
Wait.

89
00:06:30,740 --> 00:06:31,000
What?

90
00:06:31,820 --> 00:06:33,300
You're not serious, are you?

91
00:06:33,380 --> 00:06:35,800
Because I think everyone would agree you're way cooler.

92
00:06:36,220 --> 00:06:39,100
No, I'd definitely want you around if I got hurt or scared.

93
00:06:39,460 --> 00:06:40,500
How is that relevant?

94
00:06:41,640 --> 00:06:45,840
It doesn't detract from his coolness, but he is strange.

95
00:06:45,940 --> 00:06:46,880
Paper cuts stink.

96
00:06:47,420 --> 00:06:52,360
And I'd rather be described with other adjectives anyway, like cute would be nice.

97
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,720
I noticed you haven't been wearing your glasses lately.

98
00:06:56,980 --> 00:06:59,440
Yeah, they don't look all that good on me.

99
00:07:00,300 --> 00:07:01,800
So I've switched to contacts.

100
00:07:02,980 --> 00:07:06,000
I bet everything looks stunning on that gorgeous face.

101
00:07:06,220 --> 00:07:08,560
If I had a different style, I might wear them more often.

102
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:11,020
Maybe I'll check out frames after the bookstore.

103
00:07:11,220 --> 00:07:14,660
His delicate features make mine look so homely more than usual.

104
00:07:15,280 --> 00:07:16,980
You're welcome to go along with me.

105
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:18,280
Go where?

106
00:07:18,660 --> 00:07:19,640
To look at new frames.

107
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:20,720
New frames?

108
00:07:21,340 --> 00:07:22,760
You really want me along?

109
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,820
Yes, if you aren't busy, of course.

110
00:07:24,900 --> 00:07:25,840
No, I'll come.

111
00:07:26,860 --> 00:07:28,280
He asked so casually.

112
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:31,600
Who could possibly turn down such a charming invitation?

113
00:07:32,980 --> 00:07:36,540
Hey, I just thought of a funny coincidence.

114
00:07:36,540 --> 00:07:41,500
Not that it means something, but our names are kinds of trees.

115
00:07:41,880 --> 00:07:42,220
Right?

116
00:07:42,460 --> 00:07:43,500
Yanaki and Sakura.

117
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:52,460
Go for it!

118
00:07:52,460 --> 00:07:52,960
Go for it!

119
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:53,860
Go, no, wait!

120
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:55,100
Why are you running?

121
00:07:55,520 --> 00:07:56,940
Do you think they're going to sell out?

122
00:07:59,840 --> 00:08:01,560
Everything does look stunning.

123
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:06,440
Boy meets girl, boy likes girl, then boy and girl swap bodies!

124
00:08:07,260 --> 00:08:08,840
Ooh, I know that plot line.

125
00:08:09,140 --> 00:08:10,960
Yeah, I read this novel ages ago.

126
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:12,600
It is such a page-turner.

127
00:08:12,620 --> 00:08:13,160
What's it called?

128
00:08:13,580 --> 00:08:14,960
I'm her and she's me.

129
00:08:15,460 --> 00:08:16,920
Has a TV show and everything.

130
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:17,400
Huh?

131
00:08:17,820 --> 00:08:19,060
That's the first I've heard of.

132
00:08:19,400 --> 00:08:22,300
What if Hody and Miyamoto swapped bodies?

133
00:08:22,300 --> 00:08:27,760
Toru, pull your head out of your butt and talk sense.

134
00:08:28,080 --> 00:08:29,460
Oh, come on.

135
00:08:30,260 --> 00:08:31,360
Did she break?

136
00:08:31,660 --> 00:08:32,220
Hey!

137
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:35,080
Someone left their pencil case back in the council room.

138
00:08:35,580 --> 00:08:36,920
Oh, shoe most likely.

139
00:08:37,560 --> 00:08:38,880
Missing pencil case.

140
00:08:42,140 --> 00:08:43,620
Classic Ishikawa!

141
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:45,300
Pipe down.

142
00:08:45,580 --> 00:08:46,680
You're annoying me, laugh.

143
00:08:46,680 --> 00:08:48,940
What the heck?

144
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:51,200
Oh, Sengoku, there you are.

145
00:08:52,100 --> 00:08:52,940
We found the owner.

146
00:08:53,220 --> 00:08:55,140
It's one of the second years on next year's council.

147
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:57,420
Remy's relieved we figured it out.

148
00:08:57,800 --> 00:08:58,240
Oh.

149
00:08:58,820 --> 00:09:01,040
You'll find Sakura online for the cake buffet.

150
00:09:01,300 --> 00:09:03,040
Crams go before we eat cake.

151
00:09:05,460 --> 00:09:07,260
Is she okay, you think?

152
00:09:07,940 --> 00:09:10,460
She's been in La La Land for a hot minute now.

153
00:09:10,680 --> 00:09:11,400
Just leave her be.

154
00:09:12,260 --> 00:09:14,560
I was laughing because Hody switched with you-know-who.

155
00:09:14,560 --> 00:09:15,900
Then Remy and Kono did the same thing.

156
00:09:15,900 --> 00:09:18,140
Not your punching bag.

157
00:09:20,420 --> 00:09:22,720
I'm excited for the cooking class today.

158
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:24,180
Hey, that's what's up, girl.

159
00:09:25,780 --> 00:09:26,960
What is this?

160
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:31,500
Trading places gets tricky when nature calls.

161
00:09:31,860 --> 00:09:33,340
And what about bats?

162
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:34,820
Come back, Yoshikawa.

163
00:09:35,160 --> 00:09:36,300
Join the same side.

164
00:09:37,020 --> 00:09:38,560
What about the restroom, though?

165
00:09:38,660 --> 00:09:39,240
The restroom?

166
00:09:39,420 --> 00:09:40,220
What about it?

167
00:09:40,800 --> 00:09:43,260
It's rough on your kidneys if you hold it in too long.

168
00:09:43,260 --> 00:09:44,700
Just go when you gotta go.

169
00:09:44,700 --> 00:09:47,340
This question's more complex than you comprehend.

170
00:09:48,220 --> 00:09:49,220
Say what?

171
00:09:52,220 --> 00:09:53,660
Don't you ever call me Kyoko,

172
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:55,140
because it would be creepy and uncomfortable.

173
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:58,000
Kyoko.

174
00:09:59,580 --> 00:10:00,020
Kyoko.

175
00:10:02,020 --> 00:10:03,860
We're here for homework, not to goof off,

176
00:10:03,940 --> 00:10:05,520
so I'm gonna go buy some report paper.

177
00:10:05,760 --> 00:10:06,740
Have a good trip.

178
00:10:06,740 --> 00:10:09,440
While you're there, get some pencil lead.

179
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:10,080
Okay.

180
00:10:23,520 --> 00:10:23,840
Huh?

181
00:10:25,540 --> 00:10:27,640
I forgot to ask for more red pens!

182
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:40,460
I didn't think anyone else was in here with me.

183
00:10:40,620 --> 00:10:40,800
Oh.

184
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:42,680
Um, well...

185
00:10:42,680 --> 00:10:43,200
I'm sorry.

186
00:10:43,660 --> 00:10:44,400
No harm done.

187
00:10:44,540 --> 00:10:46,120
I just walked in as Hody was leaving.

188
00:10:48,760 --> 00:10:50,140
This book is cold.

189
00:10:51,220 --> 00:10:51,640
Huh?

190
00:10:51,640 --> 00:10:52,360
Uh...

191
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:54,320
Just talking to myself.

192
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:01,940
It feels that way because your hands are warm.

193
00:11:06,700 --> 00:11:08,960
When the back of his knuckles brushed mine,

194
00:11:10,020 --> 00:11:12,960
I realized just how cold Yanagi's hands are.

195
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:20,480
Yo, you finished your report?

196
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:21,840
My hands are cold.

197
00:11:21,980 --> 00:11:22,120
Hmm?

198
00:11:22,780 --> 00:11:23,500
Real cold.

199
00:11:23,840 --> 00:11:24,780
Super duper cold.

200
00:11:25,460 --> 00:11:25,900
Huh?

201
00:11:27,280 --> 00:11:28,800
You're warm enough to me.

202
00:11:29,180 --> 00:11:30,200
And again, I'm a loser.

203
00:11:30,780 --> 00:11:31,140
Hey!

204
00:11:31,360 --> 00:11:33,320
That was not an invitation to get Krabby!

205
00:11:33,680 --> 00:11:34,140
Huh?

206
00:11:35,420 --> 00:11:36,700
You are such a pain!

207
00:11:36,880 --> 00:11:38,040
What'd you expect me to do?

208
00:11:38,700 --> 00:11:41,180
At least Yanagi's gentle when he touches me,

209
00:11:41,240 --> 00:11:42,000
unlike somebody.

210
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:45,020
Are you invoking a no-touchy rule with me?

211
00:11:45,100 --> 00:11:46,760
That isn't even close to what I said!

212
00:11:47,180 --> 00:11:49,640
You are such a pain!

213
00:11:49,900 --> 00:11:50,720
Like, why is that?

214
00:11:51,280 --> 00:11:53,180
You're giving me the biggest headache right now!

215
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:54,020
Not even kidding!

216
00:11:54,500 --> 00:11:54,900
Wait!

217
00:11:55,080 --> 00:11:56,840
I thought you were kidding, Toadu!

218
00:11:57,780 --> 00:11:59,080
So, are you warm enough yet?

219
00:11:59,300 --> 00:11:59,820
Mm-hmm.

220
00:12:00,100 --> 00:12:01,460
Warm, but very exhausted.

221
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:03,100
Because you wrote that report,

222
00:12:03,360 --> 00:12:05,080
you can hit the hay as soon as you get home.

223
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:08,960
Wanna hold hands?

224
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:09,960
Not a chance!

225
00:12:10,240 --> 00:12:11,980
I doubt I'll ever understand you.

226
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:14,700
Toadu's hands are cold, too.

227
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:18,400
But they warm up pretty quick when he's with me.

228
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:24,140
Miyamura, you heading out?

229
00:12:24,520 --> 00:12:24,880
Yeah.

230
00:12:25,700 --> 00:12:27,260
I gotta make a stop at the store.

231
00:12:28,280 --> 00:12:28,860
See ya.

232
00:12:29,220 --> 00:12:29,700
Peace.

233
00:12:29,700 --> 00:12:34,440
Man, it's cold.

234
00:12:35,440 --> 00:12:35,720
Huh?

235
00:12:44,720 --> 00:12:45,800
Is this yours?

236
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:59,620
No, for real.

237
00:13:03,620 --> 00:13:04,100
Sawada,

238
00:13:04,500 --> 00:13:06,100
is there a possibility

239
00:13:06,100 --> 00:13:07,620
that you don't have friends?

240
00:13:08,600 --> 00:13:09,000
Why?

241
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:11,460
That was a yes-or-no question.

242
00:13:12,160 --> 00:13:13,240
Will you say whether or not

243
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:15,000
you're being bullied by other students, at least?

244
00:13:19,440 --> 00:13:21,440
I won't stand here and force you to talk,

245
00:13:21,620 --> 00:13:22,440
but it seemed to me

246
00:13:22,440 --> 00:13:23,640
those kids on the second floor

247
00:13:23,640 --> 00:13:24,900
threw your scarf out the window.

248
00:13:24,900 --> 00:13:26,860
If that's what happened,

249
00:13:27,600 --> 00:13:28,360
walk over to me.

250
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:41,060
Well, all right, then.

251
00:13:41,060 --> 00:13:56,760
Did you say something to them?

252
00:13:56,760 --> 00:13:57,880
Who, me?

253
00:13:57,880 --> 00:14:01,180
I didn't say a single word.

254
00:14:01,920 --> 00:14:03,960
He mouthed rot in hell, ugly cows!

255
00:14:04,220 --> 00:14:06,720
Who does that nosy nobody think he is?

256
00:14:07,820 --> 00:14:08,340
So,

257
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:11,440
you are being bullied to some extent.

258
00:14:12,620 --> 00:14:12,980
Hmm.

259
00:14:14,260 --> 00:14:15,260
At first,

260
00:14:15,400 --> 00:14:17,260
I thought we just had a difference of opinion.

261
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:19,300
And out of nowhere,

262
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:21,000
they started ignoring me.

263
00:14:22,500 --> 00:14:23,720
Sounds about right.

264
00:14:23,720 --> 00:14:28,580
You act like you know how it feels.

265
00:14:29,080 --> 00:14:30,420
But someone with your friend group

266
00:14:30,420 --> 00:14:31,440
could never relate!

267
00:14:34,140 --> 00:14:35,360
It just took time.

268
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:37,040
It's not like I went around

269
00:14:37,040 --> 00:14:38,680
begging each of them to be my friend.

270
00:14:40,420 --> 00:14:41,320
Keep your chin up.

271
00:14:42,080 --> 00:14:42,860
Things will get better.

272
00:14:44,140 --> 00:14:45,880
If those idiots are gonna ignore you,

273
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:46,900
ignore them right back.

274
00:14:47,540 --> 00:14:48,000
Know why?

275
00:14:48,560 --> 00:14:49,920
Because the ones with any brains

276
00:14:49,920 --> 00:14:51,620
will be begging to be your friends eventually.

277
00:14:52,080 --> 00:14:53,020
And you'll be the winner.

278
00:14:54,040 --> 00:14:54,480
But,

279
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:56,340
does winning even have a point?

280
00:14:57,040 --> 00:14:58,540
I figured you'd wanna win.

281
00:14:58,820 --> 00:14:59,540
I don't care.

282
00:15:03,120 --> 00:15:05,180
I forgot to tell you

283
00:15:05,180 --> 00:15:06,240
that I stepped on your scarf.

284
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:08,400
Stop!

285
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:09,700
It was an accident!

286
00:15:12,860 --> 00:15:13,560
Sawada's, like,

287
00:15:13,660 --> 00:15:14,900
really tight with the seniors.

288
00:15:15,520 --> 00:15:16,880
Guess her classmates aren't as fun

289
00:15:16,880 --> 00:15:18,460
to talk to as the older kids are.

290
00:15:18,680 --> 00:15:20,280
Yeah, I bet that's what she thinks.

291
00:15:20,620 --> 00:15:21,520
So stuck up.

292
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:23,500
She's right behind us.

293
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:24,240
Yikes.

294
00:15:26,180 --> 00:15:27,360
Why's that an issue?

295
00:15:32,180 --> 00:15:33,520
It's not that I don't want

296
00:15:33,520 --> 00:15:34,520
to get along with them.

297
00:15:35,360 --> 00:15:36,500
It's that I don't really know

298
00:15:36,500 --> 00:15:37,720
how to go about it.

299
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:41,740
So simply being in class

300
00:15:41,740 --> 00:15:43,120
makes me self-conscious.

301
00:15:43,120 --> 00:15:45,640
This wind is crazy!

302
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:46,380
Slow down!

303
00:15:46,460 --> 00:15:47,340
I love my hair!

304
00:15:49,020 --> 00:15:49,840
So chilly!

305
00:15:50,040 --> 00:15:51,040
It's too cold to be up here

306
00:15:51,040 --> 00:15:52,040
in this breezeway, Sawada!

307
00:15:52,260 --> 00:15:53,340
Come in where it's warm!

308
00:15:53,340 --> 00:15:57,420
What are you doing out there?

309
00:15:57,420 --> 00:16:00,180
Do you think I'm weird?

310
00:16:02,800 --> 00:16:03,940
Well, duh!

311
00:16:05,140 --> 00:16:07,840
But being kind of weird is awesome!

312
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:12,100
Did something happen?

313
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:13,700
Not exactly, no.

314
00:16:13,940 --> 00:16:14,540
Just think,

315
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:15,500
if you're in the weird side

316
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:16,060
of the spectrum,

317
00:16:16,440 --> 00:16:17,820
what does that make this girl?

318
00:16:17,820 --> 00:16:24,660
Here, this candy will cheer you off!

319
00:16:24,820 --> 00:16:26,260
Stag Beetle candy tastes like

320
00:16:26,260 --> 00:16:27,140
Stag Beetles too!

321
00:16:27,240 --> 00:16:28,320
Please don't feel obligated

322
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:29,080
to accept it.

323
00:16:29,140 --> 00:16:29,240
Huh?

324
00:16:29,500 --> 00:16:31,560
Oh, um, no, I want to try them.

325
00:16:31,920 --> 00:16:32,220
Aha!

326
00:16:32,220 --> 00:16:34,000
The power of Stag Beetles!

327
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:35,400
Said no one besides you.

328
00:16:35,980 --> 00:16:37,180
Apart from being weird,

329
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:39,640
do you think I'm a little too tight

330
00:16:39,640 --> 00:16:40,560
with you seniors?

331
00:16:42,780 --> 00:16:44,420
Maybe, but why is that an issue?

332
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:48,460
Because I don't really have people

333
00:16:48,460 --> 00:16:49,980
I'd consider friends

334
00:16:49,980 --> 00:16:51,500
in my own grade.

335
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:53,980
Oh, I can see why that's rough.

336
00:16:54,140 --> 00:16:56,400
Every class has to incorporate group work

337
00:16:56,400 --> 00:16:58,040
and girls form quick so fast.

338
00:16:58,040 --> 00:16:58,920
Yeah, they do!

339
00:16:59,080 --> 00:16:59,540
Mm-hmm.

340
00:16:59,860 --> 00:17:00,620
In a nutshell,

341
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:02,000
that's what it is.

342
00:17:02,220 --> 00:17:04,500
So, Ada,

343
00:17:04,800 --> 00:17:05,660
does the friend thing

344
00:17:05,660 --> 00:17:07,000
stem from classroom drama?

345
00:17:07,140 --> 00:17:07,840
Are you okay?

346
00:17:08,460 --> 00:17:09,700
Well, it's difficult,

347
00:17:09,860 --> 00:17:10,820
but I'm powering through.

348
00:17:11,140 --> 00:17:11,460
Yeah?

349
00:17:12,380 --> 00:17:12,740
Yeah.

350
00:17:13,620 --> 00:17:15,000
You can vent any time.

351
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:15,980
We'll listen to whatever

352
00:17:15,980 --> 00:17:16,820
you have to say.

353
00:17:17,420 --> 00:17:18,080
Hearing you out

354
00:17:18,080 --> 00:17:19,220
is about all we can do

355
00:17:19,220 --> 00:17:20,540
since we aren't in your class,

356
00:17:20,660 --> 00:17:22,160
but it's better than nothing, right?

357
00:17:22,480 --> 00:17:23,540
Pour your heart out!

358
00:17:24,280 --> 00:17:25,440
Thank you so much!

359
00:17:26,580 --> 00:17:27,560
Up for sampling

360
00:17:27,560 --> 00:17:28,780
some drone beetle chocolate?

361
00:17:29,120 --> 00:17:30,360
Tastes like drone beetles!

362
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:32,120
Please don't feel obligated

363
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:32,920
to accept it.

364
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:35,240
I'm not really comfortable

365
00:17:35,240 --> 00:17:36,120
in my class,

366
00:17:36,780 --> 00:17:38,760
but school's not all that bad.

367
00:17:40,380 --> 00:17:41,500
Any suggestions

368
00:17:41,500 --> 00:17:42,780
for where to post this?

369
00:17:42,900 --> 00:17:44,060
I'd say the bulletin board

370
00:17:44,060 --> 00:17:44,680
if we thought

371
00:17:44,680 --> 00:17:45,760
to reserve any space.

372
00:17:45,900 --> 00:17:46,400
Well...

373
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:47,720
Shimoda!

374
00:17:48,080 --> 00:17:48,320
Huh?

375
00:17:48,560 --> 00:17:50,020
Do you know of any free spots

376
00:17:50,020 --> 00:17:51,000
on bulletin boards?

377
00:17:51,260 --> 00:17:51,540
Yeah,

378
00:17:51,820 --> 00:17:53,100
there's one at the main entrance.

379
00:17:53,520 --> 00:17:54,540
We'll endure the wrath

380
00:17:54,540 --> 00:17:55,300
of the third years

381
00:17:55,300 --> 00:17:56,160
if we post there.

382
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:57,320
Really?

383
00:17:57,600 --> 00:17:58,560
Recruiting for clubs

384
00:17:58,560 --> 00:17:59,920
seems like quite the challenge.

385
00:18:07,180 --> 00:18:08,640
I never knew till now.

386
00:18:09,140 --> 00:18:10,320
Then guess what happened?

387
00:18:10,320 --> 00:18:12,020
Sawada!

388
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:14,700
So you were trying

389
00:18:14,700 --> 00:18:15,640
to fix that poster?

390
00:18:17,280 --> 00:18:17,720
Technically,

391
00:18:17,880 --> 00:18:18,680
it's supposed to fit

392
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:19,420
within the frame.

393
00:18:19,600 --> 00:18:19,700
Oh!

394
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:21,540
This must be the thumbtack

395
00:18:21,540 --> 00:18:22,160
that fell out!

396
00:18:22,640 --> 00:18:23,160
I'm sure.

397
00:18:23,520 --> 00:18:24,120
They couldn't push

398
00:18:24,120 --> 00:18:24,600
far enough

399
00:18:24,600 --> 00:18:25,480
into the hardwood.

400
00:18:26,320 --> 00:18:27,380
Hey, listen.

401
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:29,220
That poster?

402
00:18:29,220 --> 00:18:30,600
It belongs to some

403
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:31,700
girls I know.

404
00:18:32,660 --> 00:18:33,340
My fr...

405
00:18:33,340 --> 00:18:33,940
F...

406
00:18:33,940 --> 00:18:34,460
Fellow?

407
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:35,720
Yeah!

408
00:18:36,100 --> 00:18:37,220
My fellow classmates

409
00:18:37,220 --> 00:18:37,760
hand-painted

410
00:18:37,760 --> 00:18:38,800
that sign themselves.

411
00:18:39,140 --> 00:18:39,880
Said they're having

412
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:40,720
trouble recruiting.

413
00:18:41,720 --> 00:18:42,700
They made it big

414
00:18:42,700 --> 00:18:43,420
in order to catch

415
00:18:43,420 --> 00:18:44,140
people's attention,

416
00:18:44,340 --> 00:18:44,760
I think.

417
00:18:45,420 --> 00:18:46,560
So, um...

418
00:18:46,560 --> 00:18:47,620
Maybe...

419
00:18:47,620 --> 00:18:48,320
You could leave it

420
00:18:48,320 --> 00:18:49,000
where it is?

421
00:18:52,760 --> 00:18:54,060
It's coming down.

422
00:18:54,820 --> 00:18:55,800
But I'm gonna need

423
00:18:55,800 --> 00:18:56,240
a chair.

424
00:18:56,700 --> 00:18:57,420
Wanna grab one

425
00:18:57,420 --> 00:18:58,340
from the home ec room?

426
00:18:58,340 --> 00:18:59,600
It's right over there.

427
00:19:00,220 --> 00:19:01,500
Is it even unlocked?

428
00:19:03,800 --> 00:19:04,760
Take it down!

429
00:19:04,960 --> 00:19:06,060
Stand aside, Prez!

430
00:19:06,240 --> 00:19:06,860
Yeah, right.

431
00:19:06,940 --> 00:19:07,960
You can't reach it either.

432
00:19:11,880 --> 00:19:12,960
Don't move!

433
00:19:13,040 --> 00:19:14,020
They look like a family

434
00:19:14,020 --> 00:19:14,940
on their day off.

435
00:19:15,420 --> 00:19:16,640
Stay strong, Sengoku.

436
00:19:17,500 --> 00:19:17,920
There.

437
00:19:18,060 --> 00:19:18,660
It's off.

438
00:19:18,780 --> 00:19:19,780
Now let me down!

439
00:19:19,940 --> 00:19:21,280
Nice teamwork, you guys.

440
00:19:21,820 --> 00:19:22,800
Next stop!

441
00:19:23,280 --> 00:19:24,260
What next stop?

442
00:19:24,260 --> 00:19:25,420
Where are you taking me?

443
00:19:25,840 --> 00:19:26,700
We're done!

444
00:19:26,920 --> 00:19:27,820
Mission accomplished!

445
00:19:28,340 --> 00:19:29,920
You're heavy.

446
00:19:30,180 --> 00:19:31,620
Then hurry and let me go!

447
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:33,180
Here we are!

448
00:19:37,180 --> 00:19:40,760
The main entrance.

449
00:19:40,980 --> 00:19:41,720
May I see the sign?

450
00:19:42,460 --> 00:19:43,240
I'll post it.

451
00:19:43,620 --> 00:19:43,920
What?

452
00:19:44,340 --> 00:19:45,840
Yes, its size is eye-catching,

453
00:19:46,100 --> 00:19:47,120
but what good does that do

454
00:19:47,120 --> 00:19:48,520
if it's in a secluded spot?

455
00:19:49,340 --> 00:19:51,140
Let's move that one to the right.

456
00:19:51,520 --> 00:19:53,340
And then these two.

457
00:19:53,780 --> 00:19:54,820
And there should be space.

458
00:19:56,560 --> 00:19:56,740
Hmm?

459
00:19:58,820 --> 00:20:00,320
I thought this bulletin board

460
00:20:00,320 --> 00:20:01,980
was off-limits to us second years.

461
00:20:02,520 --> 00:20:03,280
Why's that?

462
00:20:03,520 --> 00:20:05,040
Well, because third years

463
00:20:05,040 --> 00:20:06,580
are the only ones who ever use it.

464
00:20:06,740 --> 00:20:08,580
The main entrance is a shared space.

465
00:20:09,020 --> 00:20:10,060
We won't get in trouble

466
00:20:10,060 --> 00:20:11,060
for using this board?

467
00:20:11,060 --> 00:20:12,460
Of course not.

468
00:20:12,940 --> 00:20:14,560
I guess we need to make our own sign

469
00:20:14,560 --> 00:20:15,780
that clarifies all students

470
00:20:15,780 --> 00:20:17,260
can post here no matter their year.

471
00:20:19,060 --> 00:20:19,580
Nice.

472
00:20:24,580 --> 00:20:26,640
Now every student coming through those doors

473
00:20:26,640 --> 00:20:27,840
will be sure to see in.

474
00:20:28,320 --> 00:20:29,320
Hope it gets some people

475
00:20:29,320 --> 00:20:30,400
to check out their club.

476
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:33,080
Let me make senpai!

477
00:20:33,260 --> 00:20:34,560
You're the absolute best!

478
00:20:35,120 --> 00:20:35,600
Sengoku!

479
00:20:38,860 --> 00:20:39,680
Thank you.

480
00:20:41,540 --> 00:20:42,060
Anytime.

481
00:20:43,580 --> 00:20:43,860
Oh!

482
00:20:44,180 --> 00:20:44,860
Want some candy?

483
00:20:45,460 --> 00:20:46,180
Alright now.

484
00:20:46,700 --> 00:20:48,420
How about some stag beetle chocolate?

485
00:20:52,480 --> 00:20:53,440
That's for sure.

486
00:20:53,980 --> 00:20:54,940
Tell me about it.

487
00:20:55,460 --> 00:20:56,120
Hey, Sawada.

488
00:20:58,600 --> 00:20:59,680
So is it true?

489
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:01,500
Did you really take our poster down

490
00:21:01,500 --> 00:21:02,640
and then re-hang it

491
00:21:02,640 --> 00:21:03,540
on a whole other board?

492
00:21:03,640 --> 00:21:04,880
Shimura said he saw you do it

493
00:21:04,880 --> 00:21:05,580
two days ago

494
00:21:05,580 --> 00:21:06,680
after school let out.

495
00:21:07,420 --> 00:21:08,200
He saw me?

496
00:21:10,840 --> 00:21:11,860
Um, okay.

497
00:21:12,580 --> 00:21:13,400
Signs can't overlap

498
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:14,440
the bulletin board's frame

499
00:21:14,440 --> 00:21:15,020
and yours did.

500
00:21:15,240 --> 00:21:16,560
So I moved it somewhere

501
00:21:16,560 --> 00:21:17,680
it wouldn't break any rules.

502
00:21:18,020 --> 00:21:19,700
Except it wasn't even my idea.

503
00:21:20,220 --> 00:21:21,220
A first year came by

504
00:21:21,220 --> 00:21:22,140
to check out the club.

505
00:21:24,640 --> 00:21:26,060
But that's the only bite

506
00:21:26,060 --> 00:21:27,180
we've gotten so far.

507
00:21:27,280 --> 00:21:27,560
Still,

508
00:21:27,760 --> 00:21:29,220
that was our first first year

509
00:21:29,220 --> 00:21:30,140
to show interest.

510
00:21:30,460 --> 00:21:31,020
I was like,

511
00:21:31,260 --> 00:21:31,480
what?

512
00:21:31,580 --> 00:21:32,160
When they said

513
00:21:32,160 --> 00:21:33,020
they saw the poster.

514
00:21:35,420 --> 00:21:37,420
And I was really glad too.

515
00:21:38,260 --> 00:21:39,080
Thanks for your help,

516
00:21:39,160 --> 00:21:39,480
Sawada.

517
00:21:41,880 --> 00:21:44,300
I hope the next one

518
00:21:44,300 --> 00:21:44,960
who sees it

519
00:21:44,960 --> 00:21:46,120
actually joins.

520
00:21:46,120 --> 00:21:51,520
Before I forget,

521
00:21:51,600 --> 00:21:53,740
is it also true

522
00:21:53,740 --> 00:21:54,260
that you rode

523
00:21:54,260 --> 00:21:55,080
on the student council

524
00:21:55,080 --> 00:21:56,020
president's shoulders

525
00:21:56,020 --> 00:21:57,060
to get around the school?

526
00:21:57,060 --> 00:21:57,440
Ah!

527
00:21:57,800 --> 00:21:58,240
No!

528
00:21:58,580 --> 00:21:58,940
Well,

529
00:21:59,300 --> 00:21:59,640
I mean,

530
00:21:59,700 --> 00:21:59,900
yes,

531
00:21:59,940 --> 00:22:00,500
that did happen.

532
00:22:00,780 --> 00:22:01,480
So the leader

533
00:22:01,480 --> 00:22:02,240
of the student body

534
00:22:02,240 --> 00:22:02,940
is your minion

535
00:22:02,940 --> 00:22:04,160
slash vehicle of choice?

536
00:22:04,280 --> 00:22:05,000
No way!

537
00:22:05,160 --> 00:22:06,020
And you're related

538
00:22:06,020 --> 00:22:06,860
to that bird here

539
00:22:06,860 --> 00:22:07,600
with piercings?

540
00:22:07,920 --> 00:22:09,000
All lies!

541
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:09,420
guys!

542
00:22:09,420 --> 00:22:14,160
Hiiist deles!

543
00:22:29,100 --> 00:22:32,120
Xoyang, Shnobuukuroi Kage

544
00:22:32,120 --> 00:22:35,160
Hikari wo yadoise close ayiba

545
00:22:35,160 --> 00:22:38,080
Mamoruwa koudoku ikufoza wa ni

546
00:22:38,080 --> 00:23:08,060
I'll see you next time.

547
00:23:08,080 --> 00:23:38,060
I'll see you next time.

548
00:23:38,080 --> 00:24:08,060
I'll see you next time.

